# RenoEstimate: project rules

## Deployment target
Cloudflare **Pages** via `@cloudflare/next-on-pages` (deprecated upstream in favour of OpenNext, and it declares support for Next <=15.5.2; we run 15.5.x with `legacy-peer-deps` in `.npmrc`).

- This must be a Cloudflare *Pages* project (Git integration), not a Worker. A Worker project runs `npx wrangler deploy`, whose Next.js auto-setup picks OpenNext.
- Pages settings: build command `npm run build`, build output directory `.vercel/output/static`, no deploy command. `wrangler.jsonc` declares the same via `pages_build_output_dir`.
- `npm run build` = `scripts/build.mjs`: `next build`, then `npx @cloudflare/next-on-pages`. The script has a recursion guard (the adapter runs `vercel build`, which re-runs `npm run build`): never replace it with a bare `next build && npx @cloudflare/next-on-pages`.
- `npm run build:next` is the plain `next build`. `SKIP_PAGES_ADAPTER=1 npm run build` skips the adapter (the adapter cannot run on Windows).
- Pages needs the `nodejs_compat` compatibility flag (set in wrangler.jsonc; also set it in the Pages project settings).
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables are inlined at build time: define them as build variables. Secrets (`AUTH_SECRET`, `PADDLE_API_KEY`, `PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are runtime variables/secrets.

## Edge runtime rules
- Every non-static route (route handlers and dynamic pages) must declare `export const runtime = "edge";` at the very top of the file.
- No Node built-ins (`fs`, `path`, `node:crypto`, `Buffer`, `stream`) in `app/`, `lib/`, `components/` or `hooks/`. Use Web APIs: `fetch`, `Response`, `crypto.subtle`, `TextEncoder`, `URL`.
- `lib/costEstimator.ts`, `lib/design.ts` and `lib/units.ts` are pure and must stay free of I/O and Node APIs.
- Secrets are read from `process.env` inside request handlers only, never at module scope, and never in client components (`lib/paddleServer.ts` imports `server-only`).

## Code style
- Strict TypeScript (TypeScript 5), no `any`. Modules stay small, typed and self-documenting.
